## Which Burgundy Suits Your Skin Undertone?

Yes, burgundy suits every skin tone, but not every burgundy suits every undertone. That's the reframe worth sitting with before you pick a bottle. The shade family is universal. The specific shade inside it is personal.

Cool undertones (skin with a pink, red, or blue cast, veins that read blue through the wrist) pull the most out of a blue- or purple-based burgundy. Look for rich berry or wine-red formulas that lean cool rather than brick. Warm undertones (golden, peachy, or yellow-leaning skin, greenish veins) get more from a red- or brown-based burgundy, the ones sitting closer to maroon on the spectrum. Neutral undertones have the easiest job here and can move freely across both directions without either one clashing.

