## Matte, Glossy, or Chrome - Which Finish Reads Best for Fall?

Glossy is the classic answer and matte is the modern one, and for a fall-appropriate finish on <strong>burgundy fall nails</strong>, both are correct depending on what you want your hands to do. There isn't a wrong choice here so much as two different moods wearing the same colour.

Glossy burgundy is forgiving. The shine masks minor imperfections, photographs cleanly, and reads polished in almost any setting, which is why it remains the default recommendation for a first-time burgundy manicure. Matte does something else entirely: it absorbs light instead of reflecting it, and on a colour this saturated, that absorption reads as intentional, editorial, even a little severe in a good way. It is the finish that says "cool girl" rather than "classic," and it pairs particularly well with the cozy-season, sweater-weather mood the whole trend is built around. The trade-off is durability. Matte polish chips more visibly and needs more careful upkeep than glossy, since there's no reflective top coat smoothing over the wear.

Chrome sits apart from both. A full chrome burgundy set leans metallic and festive in a way that reads closer to a December party than a September office day, so if the goal is fall specifically rather than holiday, keep chrome to a single accent nail rather than the whole hand. Against a matte or glossy burgundy base, one chrome nail adds the shine without borrowing winter's aesthetic wholesale.

