## What to Pair With Burgundy Nails This Season

Burgundy does most of its own styling work, which is part of its appeal, and <strong>burgundy fall nails</strong> need remarkably little to look finished on their own. But if you want to build on it rather than leave it alone, fall's strongest pairing is tortoiseshell, and it isn't close.

The warm amber and brown flecks in a tortoiseshell accent nail sit against burgundy's cool-to-neutral depth in a way that reads as vintage, old-money, and unmistakably autumnal all at once. It's one of the most requested combinations of the season for a reason: both patterns are already fall-coded on their own, and together they compound the effect rather than competing. If you're curious how far the tortoiseshell trend extends beyond this one pairing, <a href='/blog/fall/tortoiseshell-nails-fall'>tortoiseshell nails for fall</a> covers the full range of ways it's being worn right now.

Gold is the other dependable partner, whether as a thin outline, a scattering of foil, or a single striped accent nail. It brings warmth without pulling the whole set toward the metallic, festive territory that a full chrome finish risks. Beyond nail art, burgundy sits comfortably in fall's existing colour story: it pairs naturally with olive, rust, caramel, and chocolate brown, which means it rarely clashes with whatever else is already in a fall wardrobe.

