## How Long Does Burgundy Gel Polish Actually Last?

Burgundy gel polish lasts two to three weeks with proper application, the same range as any other gel shade, and that holds true for <strong>burgundy fall nails</strong> specifically. Colour doesn't change the chemistry. What changes is how visibly the wear shows.

Darker shades, burgundy included, tend to reveal regrowth and tip wear more clearly than lighter neutrals, simply because the contrast between fresh polish and bare nail is so much sharper. A warm beige can drift into week three looking mostly fine. A saturated burgundy will show that same amount of regrowth as a distinct line well before then. That doesn't mean the manicure has failed early. It means the maintenance window for judging "does this still look fresh" is a little shorter than it would be for a paler shade, even though the polish itself is holding on just as long. Most cream burgundy formulas reach full opacity in two coats; shimmer or jelly-leaning versions often need a third thin one to avoid streaking. Prep, thin layers, and a sealed edge do more for longevity than the shade you've chosen ever will.

